balesdk talks to Bale through aiobale (PyPI: aiobale-py), an MIT-licensed
library that implements Bale's internal protocol. All of the protocol work -
the reverse engineering, the message definitions, the connection handling - is
theirs. balesdk adds a stable, tested layer on top. Please credit and support
that project.

  aiobale  https://github.com/aminmadaniofficial/aiobale  (MIT, Amin Madani)

The design borrows ideas from WAHA (WhatsApp HTTP API: sessions, webhooks, an
API key) and rubpy (a personal-account Rubika client). No code is copied.

balesdk is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or connected to Bale.
